  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is firing on all cylinders while Hicksville posted a concerning miss yesterday\u2014and the gap is entirely capacity-driven, not demand.\n\nPort Washington delivered $3,402 yesterday (up 18% YoY, up 21% in grooming) with four groomers hitting $448/groomer-day. That's 7% below your 30-day baseline, but the real story is volume: you're up 45% YTD both in revenue and appointments against last year. MTD you're tracking +8.7% versus DOW-adjusted expectation\u2014real performance, not calendar luck. Add-on attach climbed to 52% from 41%, showing strong upsell discipline. One flag: retail and add-ons are both undersized relative to grooming growth, suggesting front-of-house has room to lean in on suggestive selling. Your lapse pool of 469 customers represents $296K in annual opportunity\u2014worth a reactivation push this quarter.\n\nHicksville cratered yesterday (down 17% total, down 26% in grooming) with only two groomers on the floor. That capacity constraint is the entire story: at $470/groomer-day, your two groomers actually outpaced baseline (+13%), but you're scheduled for zero groomers today and one tomorrow, which means the week ahead is structurally weak (18 groomer-days over seven days vs. Port's 38). Retail spiked 78%, which is noise\u2014add-on revenue collapsed from $185 to $55 because you lacked the grooming capacity to support it. The real issue: Hicksville is running skeleton crew. Inventory across both locations shows 20 items out of stock (non-critical), but your top reorder priorities are bleeding: X-Small Treat Table and Shanti's Medical Journey both deeply negative. Restock these immediately.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Port Washington has 1 groomer and 7.0 bather hours today, 6 groomers and 7.0 bather hours tomorrow, with 38 groomer-days scheduled over the next 7 days; Hicksville has 0 groomers and 0 bather hours today, 1 groomer and 0 bather hours tomorrow, with only 18 groomer-days scheduled over the next 7 days\u2014Hicksville's coverage is the constraint limiting your Augustrevenue potential.**"
